# Every timing patch

This is a standing user requirement for all future timing patches, including
small boundary edits. Follow the complete
[AGENTS.md checklist](../../AGENTS.md#landing-timings-lab--github-timing-patches)
and [Timings Lab workflow](../../docs/TIMINGS_LAB.md) without another reminder.

1. Compare the patch with currently delivered rows. Trace disagreements through
   source, cleaner, corrections, repairs, finalization and reviewed holds.
2. Audit each defect class across the complete applicable corpus and reciters,
   including owned/held rows and analogous open/closed issues. Preserve genuine
   repeats and use correct rows as negative controls.
3. Run actual dual-model acoustic inference for ambiguous topology. Use sequence
   scores for topology and start residuals plus waveform tails for boundaries.
   Follow the existing gates; never infer Bluetooth offsets or claim listening
   that did not occur.
4. Fix the class with a reusable, calibrated detector and regression cases.
   Exact-verse fixtures or source-guarded entries alone do not prove a class fix.
   Keep any necessary human exception explicit and uncertain rows at baseline.
5. Record predicates, source revisions, counts, every candidate disposition,
   evidence paths, errors and uncertainty in the repair report or PR. Label
   unfinished class audits as partial and track them in
   [OUTSTANDING.md](../../tools/timing_verdicts/OUTSTANDING.md).

Keep full QF timing packs and alignment JSONL private. Acoustic acceptance and
an APK build do not replace authenticated-source review or runtime publication.
